Both files are **unmodified** verbatim copies of the upstream files at the
commit above. Any local fix must be sent upstream first; if a local patch ever
becomes unavoidable, record it here and keep it as a separate .patch file so
the next update can be replayed.

Updating
--------

    SHA=$(curl -s https://api.github.com/repos/jonoton/cpp-tui/commits/main \
          | sed -n 's/.*"sha": "\([0-9a-f]\{40\}\)".*/\1/p' | head -1)
    curl -L -o cpptui.hpp https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jonoton/cpp-tui/$SHA/cpptui.hpp
    curl -L -o LICENSE    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jonoton/cpp-tui/$SHA/LICENSE

Then update the commit, date, sizes and sha256 above.

Usage notes
-----------

Header-only, no dependency, no object file: only an include path is needed
(-I$(top_srcdir)/src/lib/cpptui, added to src/bin/tools/Makefile.am).

cpptui.hpp must only be included from .cpp files of the TUI, never from a
header exposed to the rest of the tree: it is 18k lines and it costs roughly
+10 s of compile time and +650 MB of compiler RSS per translation unit that
includes it (measured with the project's own CXXFLAGS, gcc 12, aarch64).

The header produces 30 warnings with the project's warning flags (29 -Wshadow,
1 -Wunused-variable). Include it through a thin local wrapper that wraps the
#include in `#pragma GCC diagnostic push / ignored "-Wshadow" / ignored
"-Wunused-variable" / pop`, so the tree stays at zero warnings without
weakening the flags for our own code.
